Anyone try to port Nethack to a Timex-Sinclair ZX-81 yet?
Of course, you'd have to turn off several features to reduce
the size of the executable.  My ZX-81 has 1K, but I've been
thinking of upgrading to 16K.

How about porting it to the Cosmic Elf?  Of course, all screen
activity would have to be reduced to a 2 digit hex code.
(3F = You are frozen by the floating eye's gaze, etc)
Plus, the command keys would have to be remapped to a 16
key keymap.  And if you don't have a storage device, the
executable will have to be reentered by hand every time you
wish to play.  But these are minor inconveniences.

I can see it now.  Nethack.  The ONLY program ported to every
known computer in existence.  :-)


